{
	title: "Wind Turbine",
	icon: "ic2:te 1 21",
	x: 3.4d,
	y: 4.9d,
	text: [
		"§oNot to be confused with Wind Mill.§r\nWind Turbine is one of the most poweful methods of EU generation in IC2.\n\n§8[§6Setup§8]§r\nWind Turbine must be placed at a high Y level (best at §7Y=160§r) and requires a rotor and a Kinetic Generator to function.\n\n§8[§6Rotors§8]§r\nThere are multiple rotors to choose from, but it's recommended to go straight to §8Carbon§r one - it's the most effective and slightly cheaper than Steel rotor.\n\nAll rotors have durability and will be worn out with time, but the time period is extremely long - one rotor should last for several real days of continuous use.\n\nCarbon rotor produces 300-400 EU/t depending on the weather.\n\n§8[§6Efficient energy transfer§8]§r\nYou can use HV transformers to step-up voltage to 2048 EU/t and transfer energy with lesser losses from Wind Turbine to your base! Don't forget to step it down, though."
	],
